1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,450
How to Manage Your Time Better.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:06,012
Time management is not about cramming more into a day.

3
00:00:06,012 --> 00:00:09,887
It is about ensuring the most important tasks are completed.

4
00:00:09,887 --> 00:00:19,012
Identifying the two or three highest-priority tasks and completing them first, before checking messages or social media, is the core principle.

5
00:00:19,012 --> 00:00:22,225
This approach is sometimes called eating the frog.

6
00:00:22,225 --> 00:00:29,050
Time blocking — scheduling specific tasks for specific hours — works better than open-ended to-do lists.

7
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:33,287
Every yes to something unimportant is a no to something that matters.

8
00:00:33,287 --> 00:00:42,562
Protecting peak energy hours, typically a 2- to 3-hour window of sharpest cognition, for the most important work yields the greatest results.

